{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791624460,"nonce":"Ysh6i8ymvsbHnjS3ABOj4gcSJsI=","title":"var() inside @keyframes","message":"A @keyframes declaration that uses var() is reported, \"@keyframes NAME: var() in \\\"PROPERTY\\\" is not supported\", and left out (native/src/motion/keyframes.rs, part of 35f7bd0c1ec8685e615f6ffdd92e84d69d9de4ea0a5820e8da6694a414ca344f). Keyframe blocks are read from the sheet as written; nothing resolves their variables, unlike rule declarations, which the cascade resolves before the host sees them.\n\nThe resolution exists in blinc_abi, Cascade::substitute (src/css/cascade.rs), but it is private. Exposing it (resolve a value against an element's computed values, the sheets' :root variables and the theme) would let keyframes use theme tokens, such as a colour that follows the scheme. That is a blinc_abi change shared with the other SDK, so agree the API with that repo's owner first.\n\nAcceptance: @keyframes pulse { from { background: var(--primary) } ... } animates in the theme's colour, and follows a scheme switch for animations started after it.","files":null}]}